There is no single federal address update. USPS says a Change of Address only reroutes mail at the Post Office. You still must update government agencies yourself. USPS Change of Address

Do not send me your address or ID numbers. Use each agency’s own process.

USPS (mail forwarding only)

• Online or at a Post Office (PS Form 3575). Identity check required; online has a small fee.
• Does not replace agency updates.
• Source: usps.com/manage/forward.htm

Notify separately (USPS does not replace this)

Social Security (and Medicare address)

• Retirement, survivors, disability, or Medicare: update in my Social Security (My Profile). Or call 1-800-772-1213.
• Medicare address is changed through SSA, even if you do not get SSA payments. HHS
• SSI: SSA says you generally cannot change address online the same way; contact SSA. SSA FAQ

IRS

• File your next return with the new address, or Form 8822 (8822-B for business).
• USPS/NCOA may update IRS records, but IRS still says notify them (checks may not forward). IRS address changes

USCIS

• USPS will not change your USCIS address. Green cards and EADs are not forwarded.
• Most people: USCIS online account / E-COA; noncitizens generally must report a move within 10 days. USCIS how to change address · USCIS alert
• Affidavit-of-support sponsors: Form I-865 within 30 days.

Immigration court (EOIR) and ICE

• Separate from USCIS and USPS. File Form EOIR-33 within 5 working days; serve DHS/ICE. Court will not take a new address from other papers.

VA

• VA.gov profile covers many benefits (health, disability, pension, education, claims, VR&E). VA change address
• Some VA records (for example insurance) stay separate; contact that office.

Federal retirement / TSP

• OPM annuity: Retirement Services Online
• TSP: still employed → your agency (or military TSP section in myPay). Separated → TSP My Account. TSP mailing address

U.S. passport

• Existing passport: no address update needed. Pending application: call 877-487-2778. State Department

Selective Service (if you must stay registered, generally until Jan. 1 of the year you turn 26): update SSS separately. USA.gov

Federal student loans: update StudentAid.gov / your loan servicer; USPS does not do this. Official hub: studentaid.gov

Sometimes updated from another federal system (not a substitute)

• IRS ← USPS NCOA: possible match; IRS still wants a direct notice.
• SSA ← NCOA: SSA may match names/addresses; still update SSA yourself. SSA POMS NCOA
• SSA earnings statement address ← IRS until you claim benefits (embassy SSA page).
• Medicare ← SSA (not a separate Medicare address file for the official address).
• TSP (current employees) ← agency/payroll, not USPS.

Important records USPS does not update

USCIS case/secure cards, EOIR court notices, VA profile, OPM annuity, TSP (especially after you leave federal service), IRS reliably, SSA/Medicare reliably, Selective Service, student aid, pending passport mail.

I could not verify one master list of every federal file. If you name a program (SSI, VA insurance, FEHB, etc.), I can look up that agency’s steps.

