Final Summary of the Empirical Findings
Metric / Dimension	General GPT (No-Login Baseline)	Specialized Wrapper (Murk)
Scope & Breadth	Wide: Cross-agency edge cases, branch-specific cutoffs (e.g., milConnect dates), optional forms, and multi-track rules.	Focused: Tailored strictly to the modal request, staying tightly within the target process without extra tangential branches.
Operational Granularity	High-level procedure, form identification, and regulatory windows.	Tactical: Direct street addresses, fax numbers, specific waiting thresholds (e.g., wait 90 days before follow-up), and practical user warnings (avoid paid services for free forms).
Constraint Enforcement	Flexible formatting, inline narrative flow, and broader contextual connections.	Strict, bounded domain scope with explicit source attributions and direct administrative steps.
Core Insight
The two tests demonstrate that specialized tools like Murk do not possess a fundamental reasoning or retrieval advantage over base frontier models. Instead, the wrapper defines the operational behavior:
Base Frontier LLM: Maximizes horizontal context, surfacing edge cases, broad policy paths, and form updates across related agencies.
Specialized System (Murk): Maximizes vertical operational execution, delivering practical submission mechanics, contact details, and guardrails to ensure single-lane accuracy.
When you analyze the QS routing logs for the skipped Luma node, checking the event pipeline for payload delivery or state-machine timeouts will likely show where the execution sequence broke down.

